{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-27-Nov-2025-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 18, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "If tan A = 1, then find the value of sin A + cos A.", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": "C"}, {"n": 2, "text": "The market value of Amal’s investment rises successively by 5% in 2021, 6% in 2022, and 10% in 2023. If the initial value was ₹5,50,000, what will be its value (in ₹) at the end of 2023?", "options": [{"text": "6,75,800", "added": false}, {"text": "6,75,365", "added": false}, {"text": "6,73,365", "added": false}, {"text": "6,75,900", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "6,73,365"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Simplify the following:", "options": [{"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "60"}, {"n": 4, "text": "A and B working together can do a piece of work in 6 days. B alone can do the same work in 15 days. How long (in days) will A alone take to do double the work?", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "20"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The number of prime numbers lying between 374 and 384 is:", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "types-of-numbers", "key_answer": "2"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A brother is 6 years older than his sister. The sum of their present ages is 38 years. What will be the age (in years) of the sister after 15 years from now?", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "31", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": "31"}, {"n": 7, "text": "A shopkeeper marks the price of an article at ₹5,670. Find the cost price if after allowing a discount of 28% he still gains 26% on the cost price.", "options": [{"text": "₹3,153", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,216", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,240", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,225", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": "₹3,240"}, {"n": 8, "text": "Amit and Deeksha together invested ₹15,700 in a business. At the end of the year, out of a total profit of ₹6,000, Amit's share was ₹2,100. How much was Amit's investment?", "options": [{"text": "₹6,330", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,960", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,545", "added": false}, {"text": "₹5,495", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "₹5,495"}, {"n": 9, "text": "The cost of fencing a square field at ₹15/m is ₹18,000. Find the cost of fencing the same field at ₹11 per 100 m.", "options": [{"text": "₹138", "added": false}, {"text": "₹146", "added": false}, {"text": "₹142", "added": false}, {"text": "₹132", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": "₹132"}, {"n": 10, "text": "A person saves 60% of his income. If his expenditure is ₹400, then his income (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "160", "added": false}, {"text": "240", "added": false}, {"text": "1,040", "added": false}, {"text": "1,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": "1,000"}, {"n": 11, "text": "The HCF of two numbers is 23 and their sum is 161. The possible pair(s) of these numbers is/are:", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": "3"}, {"n": 12, "text": "A toy is in the form of a cone mounted on a hemisphere, both having the same radius of 7 cm. If the volume of the conical part is equal to the volume of the hemispherical part, what is the total height of the toy?", "options": [{"text": "21 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "14 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "35 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "28 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": "21 cm"}, {"n": 13, "text": "If an item marked at ₹3,650 is sold for ₹730, what is the discount percentage?", "options": [{"text": "80%", "added": false}, {"text": "82%", "added": false}, {"text": "79%", "added": false}, {"text": "78%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "80%"}, {"n": 14, "text": "A shopkeeper sold an article for ₹85.50 at a profit of 12.5%. Had he sold it for ₹81.70, then what would be his profit or loss percentage?", "options": [{"text": "8.5% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "7.25% loss", "added": false}, {"text": "7.5% profit", "added": false}, {"text": "8.5% profit", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "7.5% profit"}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": "2"}, {"n": 16, "text": "Find the simple interest (in ₹) on ₹4,000 at 6% per annum rate of interest for the period from 19 February 2024 to 20 April 2024.", "options": [{"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "40"}, {"n": 17, "text": "Rajiv and Sachin started a business, investing amounts of ₹160 and ₹1,690, respectively. If Rajiv's share in the profit earned by them is ₹720, what is the total profit (in ₹) earned by them together?", "options": [{"text": "8,325", "added": false}, {"text": "8,395", "added": false}, {"text": "8,361", "added": false}, {"text": "8,454", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "8,325"}, {"n": 18, "text": "The arithmetic mean of the observations 76, 28, 79, 17, 33, 95, 83, 30 and 27 is:", "options": [{"text": "52", "added": false}, {"text": "61", "added": false}, {"text": "47", "added": false}, {"text": "46", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Elementary Statistics", "sub": "mean-median-mode", "key_answer": "52"}]}